# rlbootsmann.msg - Bo Harlan, bosun of the tanker (San Francisco, the Bilge)
# Plain ASCII only: the English Fallout 2 fonts have no umlauts or typographic quotes.

{100}{}{(A heavy man with a tattooed neck leans on the bar that nobody tends.) Bo Harlan, bosun on the tanker. The Shi think they own the docks. The tanker floats. Whoever drinks here drinks with us, whether Wen likes it or not.}
{101}{}{[Speech] Back me. The Bilge opens without the Shi.}
{102}{}{(Harlan raises his cup.) Still afloat.}
{103}{}{Your people could store things in the Bilge. Things the Shi don't need to see.}
{104}{}{See you, Harlan.}
{105}{}{Boat?}
{110}{}{(He laughs and slaps the bar.) No tribute, no Shi. The tanker has your back, and our smugglers have a room behind the old bilge pumps. Wen will be sour for a year. (He whistles.) Kwan! She's been sitting out there for days. She'll run it for you.}
{120}{}{(Harlan spits on the floor next to your boots.) Shi rat. Every name we said in here went to the palace. Get away from me.}
{130}{}{(He grins.) Behind the old bilge pumps. Build it, and the tanker's goods come in at night. The Shi won't like it when they find out.}

# Look
{300}{}{A heavy man with a tattooed neck and a tin cup.}
{301}{}{Bo Harlan, bosun of the tanker. He decides who on the docks drinks with the tanker crew.}
